                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Sorry, gotta give this a no-go.  I bought it a long time ago and had in my inventory.  Decided to give it a try.  I enjoy first person, atmospheric, exploration stuff.  \n\nI got through chapter one ok.  The environment is very dark, often walking into corners because it was so dark I couldn't tell if anything was there.  Experience I had is mostly linear exploration of an abandoned ship/station, and running around clicking lots of things without knowing why, to find what was interactable to open doors, find tools, click buttons, turn on systems, etc to enable advancement.  Sometimes the game locks you in area to let you know the pieces of the puzzle are there so you don't go wandering away, but it's also an indication that you may not be aware what you're looking for.  Just keep looking around.  The layout of ship/station really didn't make sense to me - it was huge, spread out, with long halls so I didn't have a proper sense of space.\n\nI stopped/abandoned at chapter 2 because I could not make a platforming leap that was required to advance the story.  It's ok.  Encouraged me to move on to something else.",
